# Every acceptance id in PHASE-1-PLAN.md that this repo's CI reports on, with
# where it's checked: a workflow's name, or "manual" for a check on the NUC.
# Grows stage by stage (ADR-019). test/agentv/report reads this.

S0.1  iso       a tagged release's ISO installs in CI and boots to the TV setup welcome screen
S0.2  manual    the NUC boots from the ISO to the welcome screen, with no boot password (agentv selftest S0.2)
S0.3  manual    NetworkManager brings up the setup hotspot on the NUC's Wi-Fi (agentv selftest S0.3)
S0.4  iso       the AgenTV logo in the installer, boot splash and screensaver; no Omarchy file edited
S0.5  agentv-os the nightly run updates a box from the last release in place
S0.6  sync      a new Omarchy stable tag gets a sync pull request that merges itself only when green
S0.7  agentv-os the nightly run signs tested.json, and a box holds back what it doesn't list
S1.1  iso       a cold boot lands in the TV session on the welcome page, with nothing of Omarchy's desktop in it
S1.2  manual    10 minutes of a streaming service at 720p in the services' Chromium, no stutter, no fan (agentv selftest S1.2)
S1.3  iso       the TV to Omarchy's desktop and back each take under 10 s
S1.4  agentv-plugin the Back to TV plugin passes omarchy plugin validate (the repo isn't made yet)
S1.5  manual    the TV session check: 60 fps, an app and home again, a toast over a film, Steam in its gamescope (agentv selftest S1.5)
S1.6  iso       no window takes the screen unless the daemon puts it in front: a new window, a home screen crash, an update
S1.7  iso       signing in to a test page in the services' Chromium shows no browser prompt: no Save password, translate, notification or autofill bubble
